* kindling proof model
*
* 3 variables, 1 constraints
*
* --- x1 in [0, 7], the model's x1 ---
* x1 = 4*x1b2 + 2*x1b1 + 1*x1b0
*
* x1ge{v} means x1 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x1ge{v} ==> 4*x1b2 + 2*x1b1 + 1*x1b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x1ge{v} <== 4*x1b2 + 2*x1b1 + 1*x1b0 >= v.
@x1ge1_up @x1ge1_dn x1ge1 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 1 ;
@x1ge2_up @x1ge2_dn x1ge2 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 2 ;
@x1ge3_up @x1ge3_dn x1ge3 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 3 ;
@x1ge4_up @x1ge4_dn x1ge4 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 4 ;
@x1ge5_up @x1ge5_dn x1ge5 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 5 ;
@x1ge6_up @x1ge6_dn x1ge6 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 6 ;
@x1ge7_up @x1ge7_dn x1ge7 <==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= 7 ;
* x1eq{v} means x1 = v, which is x1ge{v} and not x1ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x1eq0_up @x1eq0_dn x1eq0 <==> 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq1_up @x1eq1_dn x1eq1 <==> 1 x1ge1 1 ~x1ge2 >= 2 ;
@x1eq2_up @x1eq2_dn x1eq2 <==> 1 x1ge2 1 ~x1ge3 >= 2 ;
@x1eq3_up @x1eq3_dn x1eq3 <==> 1 x1ge3 1 ~x1ge4 >= 2 ;
@x1eq4_up @x1eq4_dn x1eq4 <==> 1 x1ge4 1 ~x1ge5 >= 2 ;
@x1eq5_up @x1eq5_dn x1eq5 <==> 1 x1ge5 1 ~x1ge6 >= 2 ;
@x1eq6_up @x1eq6_dn x1eq6 <==> 1 x1ge6 1 ~x1ge7 >= 2 ;
@x1eq7_up @x1eq7_dn x1eq7 <==> 1 x1ge7 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x2 in [0, 7], the model's x2 ---
* x2 = 4*x2b2 + 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0
*
* x2ge{v} means x2 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x2ge{v} ==> 4*x2b2 + 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x2ge{v} <== 4*x2b2 + 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0 >= v.
@x2ge1_up @x2ge1_dn x2ge1 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 1 ;
@x2ge2_up @x2ge2_dn x2ge2 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 2 ;
@x2ge3_up @x2ge3_dn x2ge3 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 3 ;
@x2ge4_up @x2ge4_dn x2ge4 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 4 ;
@x2ge5_up @x2ge5_dn x2ge5 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 5 ;
@x2ge6_up @x2ge6_dn x2ge6 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 6 ;
@x2ge7_up @x2ge7_dn x2ge7 <==> 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 7 ;
* x2eq{v} means x2 = v, which is x2ge{v} and not x2ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x2eq0_up @x2eq0_dn x2eq0 <==> 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq1_up @x2eq1_dn x2eq1 <==> 1 x2ge1 1 ~x2ge2 >= 2 ;
@x2eq2_up @x2eq2_dn x2eq2 <==> 1 x2ge2 1 ~x2ge3 >= 2 ;
@x2eq3_up @x2eq3_dn x2eq3 <==> 1 x2ge3 1 ~x2ge4 >= 2 ;
@x2eq4_up @x2eq4_dn x2eq4 <==> 1 x2ge4 1 ~x2ge5 >= 2 ;
@x2eq5_up @x2eq5_dn x2eq5 <==> 1 x2ge5 1 ~x2ge6 >= 2 ;
@x2eq6_up @x2eq6_dn x2eq6 <==> 1 x2ge6 1 ~x2ge7 >= 2 ;
@x2eq7_up @x2eq7_dn x2eq7 <==> 1 x2ge7 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x3 in [0, 7], the model's x3 ---
* x3 = 4*x3b2 + 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0
*
* x3ge{v} means x3 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x3ge{v} ==> 4*x3b2 + 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x3ge{v} <== 4*x3b2 + 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0 >= v.
@x3ge1_up @x3ge1_dn x3ge1 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 1 ;
@x3ge2_up @x3ge2_dn x3ge2 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 2 ;
@x3ge3_up @x3ge3_dn x3ge3 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 3 ;
@x3ge4_up @x3ge4_dn x3ge4 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 4 ;
@x3ge5_up @x3ge5_dn x3ge5 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 5 ;
@x3ge6_up @x3ge6_dn x3ge6 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 6 ;
@x3ge7_up @x3ge7_dn x3ge7 <==> 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 7 ;
* x3eq{v} means x3 = v, which is x3ge{v} and not x3ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x3eq0_up @x3eq0_dn x3eq0 <==> 1 ~x3ge1 >= 1 ;
@x3eq1_up @x3eq1_dn x3eq1 <==> 1 x3ge1 1 ~x3ge2 >= 2 ;
@x3eq2_up @x3eq2_dn x3eq2 <==> 1 x3ge2 1 ~x3ge3 >= 2 ;
@x3eq3_up @x3eq3_dn x3eq3 <==> 1 x3ge3 1 ~x3ge4 >= 2 ;
@x3eq4_up @x3eq4_dn x3eq4 <==> 1 x3ge4 1 ~x3ge5 >= 2 ;
@x3eq5_up @x3eq5_dn x3eq5 <==> 1 x3ge5 1 ~x3ge6 >= 2 ;
@x3eq6_up @x3eq6_dn x3eq6 <==> 1 x3ge6 1 ~x3ge7 >= 2 ;
@x3eq7_up @x3eq7_dn x3eq7 <==> 1 x3ge7 >= 1 ;
*
* x1 + x2 + x3 <= 9
@lin1 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 4 x2b2 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 4 x3b2 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 <= 9 ;
